     "parsed_output": null,
     "text": "Round 1 used `TILE=8192`, giving 2560 blocks and 21.8 ms. For this round I doubled the tile to 16384 elements (1280 blocks). `n` divides evenly by 16384, so there are no partial tiles.\n\nThe aim is to cut how often a block is launched and torn down, and to keep more loads in flight per block. The cost is a coarser tail at the end of the grid. Whether that trade pays off is untested until it is timed.\n\nEverything else is unchanged:\n- **Kernel:** one launch, one tile per block.\n- **Edge handling:** bounds-padded loads and bounds-clipped stores.\n- **Precision:** the add is done in fp16.\n\n```python title=\"impl_cutile.py\"\nimport torch\nimport cuda.tile as ct\n\nConstInt = ct.Constant[int]\n\n# Fixed configuration literals\n_TILE = 16384\n\n_CONFIG = {\"TILE\": _TILE}\n\n\n@ct.kernel\ndef _vector_add_kernel(x, y, out, TILE: ConstInt):\n    bid = ct.bid(0)\n    a = ct.load(x, (bid,), (TILE,), padding_mode=ct.PaddingMode.ZERO)\n    b = ct.load(y, (bid,), (TILE,), padding_mode=ct.PaddingMode.ZERO)\n    ct.store(out, (bid,), a + b)\n\n\ndef run(x, y):\n    xf = x.view(-1)\n    yf = y.view(-1)\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    of = out.view(-1)\n    n = xf.numel()\n    if n == 0:\n        return out\n    grid = (ct.cdiv(n, _TILE),)\n    ct.launch(torch.cuda.current_stream(), grid, _vector_add_kernel,\n              (xf, yf, of, _TILE))\n    return out\n\n\ndef get_last_config() -> dict:\n    return dict(_CONFIG)\n```",
     "type": "text"
    }
